s("S0149","News-site header (logo, nav, Sign In and Subscribe buttons) over a four-line article paragraph (top y0.2-0.5); large black wordmark with swoosh at left-bottom (x0.1-0.65, y0.62-0.78) and rocket at right (x0.65-0.83); yellow highlight sweeps a line (SUB016).","White canvas with webpage screenshot","Article is a raster UI; rocket in thick-outline cartoon.","Article body ~2.3% frame height grey; wordmark huge black spaced caps ~8%.","Reuters; 'My News' 'Sign In' 'Subscribe'; 'Lower costs may attract more would-be space explorers. But rocket revenue was perhaps $4 billion last year and SpaceX has historically run the business at around breakeven. Rival Lockheed Martin (LMT.N) is valued at two times estimated revenue. Even if the unit's growth prospects deserve a much higher multiple of, say, five times revenue, the resulting $20 billion price tag is a rounding error in SpaceX's valuation.'","","Article text as evidence; wordmark and rocket as large graphic.","STATIC 2D","Hard cut (wipe-like) from EP0215 end ~f5551; exit EP0216.","Evidence quote on rocket revenue being small.","OBSERVED: highlight sweep.","HIGH","Rocket from S0145.","Place a webpage header and paragraph at top, big wordmark and rocket below, sweep a yellow highlight over one line.","Flat scene: wide white article block with header bar and four lines of grey text at top, big bold black wordmark with swoosh at lower left, cartoon rocket at lower right, yellow highlight bar over one line.","F5 screenshot+character")
